<p>President Trump said the U.S. Navy is clearing Iranian mines from the Strait of Hormuz as Washington tries to restart shipping through one of the world’s most important oil transit routes. The operation follows disruption in the strait that pushed up energy prices and raised concern about wider economic effects. France, Germany, and Turkiye were cited as supporting efforts that could help reopen the waterway after the ceasefire extension. The broader picture remains tense. The Financial Times reported that mine-clearing could take weeks even if the U.S. gets help from hesitant European allies. Dawn reported that Iran has demanded the United States lift its blockade of Iranian ports and warned it would respond if what it called U.S. “piracy” continued, even as France, Germany, and Turkiye backed efforts that could help reopen the waterway after the ceasefire extension.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/w81OawDKlSGpDD-hhI87fGrkhtWbW1nqKc764oZADLmhKt1FinXa7-k6cj92mmnBH4bTcX_I5tI8LDfoFA218GdeC1brtLUr3AD1BkH2asxy' alt='Oil tankers pass through the Strait of Hormuz, on December 21, 2018.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>European help: Germany and Turkiye agreed to de-mining missions, while the Financial Times said broader European support has been reluctant even though outside help could speed clearance</li><li>Ceasefire hurdle: Dawn said the ceasefire between the U.S. and Iran was recently extended, but Hormuz remains a central obstacle to reviving broader talks</li><li>Port blockade: According to Dawn, the U.S. earlier blockaded Iranian ports to curb Iran’s oil exports and turned back more than 30 ships leaving those ports</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: President Trump said the U.S. Navy is actively clearing Iranian mines as part of Washington’s latest push to get maritime traffic moving again through the strait. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-says-its-clearing-iranian-mines-in-latest-push-to-open-the-strait-of-hormuz'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iran’s military central command said Tehran would respond if the U.S. kept blockading Iranian ports, calling those actions “banditry” and “piracy.” (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995116/hormuz-stays-flashpoint-amid-reopening-move'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>France: President Emmanuel Macron said he wants the strait fully reopened in the coming days and weeks. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995116/hormuz-stays-flashpoint-amid-reopening-move'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysis: The newspaper said clearing mines from the Gulf waterway will likely take weeks even with allied support, underscoring the practical limits of a rapid reopening. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/78a983c8-6ed5-42f3-b794-7fed9ee189ed'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/78a983c8-6ed5-42f3-b794-7fed9ee189ed'>How to demine the Strait of Hormuz</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/us-says-it%27s-hunting-for-explosive-mines-in-latest-push-to-open-the-strait-of-hormuz'>Trump says U.S. clearing mines in latest push to open the Strait of Hormuz</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-says-its-clearing-iranian-mines-in-latest-push-to-open-the-strait-of-hormuz'>U.S. says it&#x27;s clearing Iranian mines in latest push to open the Strait of Hormuz</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995116/hormuz-stays-flashpoint-amid-reopening-move'>Hormuz stays flashpoint amid reopening move</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>